// BUG 1 — x86_emit.oo missing 6 imports (MED)
//
// Six of fourteen x86_emit_*.oo helpers are on disk but never
// imported. x86_emit_stream cannot reach them. Dead code.
//
// Evidence:
//   ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo:15-23 imports 7: fold, fn, rsi, str,
//     greet, walk, sys (+ token_fmt, secret_check).
//   Disk inventory: 14 x86_emit_*.oo exist. 6 missing imports:
//     x86_emit_alu, x86_emit_bind, x86_emit_ctl, x86_emit_frame,
//     x86_emit_harv, x86_emit_span (orphans).
//   x86_emit.oo:25-61 stream body has no calls to those six.
//
// Fix:
//   File: ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo
//   Action: after line 23, add 6 imports (alphabetical): the 6
//     orphan names listed above.
//   Wire each into x86_emit_stream after line 60 with a list_len
//   probe. Add an x86_match_<role> helper inside each file if
//   none exists; default returns list_new().
//   Pass: x86_emit.oo still folds hello.oo; grep -c '^import' == 14.
//   Fail: any import referencing a helper that does not exist.
//
// Acceptance:
//   1. ./oodac/oodac emit-x86 fixtures/hello.oo | grep -q 'main:'
//   2. grep -c '^import' ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo == 14.
//   3. wc -l ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo <= 80.
//
// Rollback: git checkout HEAD -- ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo.

// BUG 2 — llvm_emit_method.oo:146 .len() live ERR (HIGH)
//
// llvm_apply_method handles .len() for %OoSList, %OoIList, %OoStr.
// Any other rty hits the fail-closed ERR. Survey says the live
// rty can be a Result wrapper that needs the byval list path.
//
// Evidence:
//   ooda/oodac/llvm_emit_method.oo:122-148 is the .len() block.
//   :139 emits byval call only for %OoSList / %OoIList.
//   :142-145 handles %OoStr.
//   :146 ERRs: "ERR\tllvm_emit\t.len() needs String or List".
//
// Fix:
//   File: ooda/oodac/llvm_emit_method.oo
//   Action: at line 146, replace the single ERR with a normalized
//   branch BEFORE the ERR. Pattern (in OODA):
//     if rty == "%OoResS" { emit @oo_chars_len(%OoStr recv); }
//     if rty starts with "%OoS" or "%OoIL" {
//         alloca rty; store; emit
//         call i64 @oo_<slist|ilist>_len(rty* byval(rty) slot);
//     }
//     // keep the original ERR for the truly unknown case
//   The result methods on lines 67-100 and unwrap on 101-121 are
//   unchanged. The :139 byval block can be extracted into a small
//   helper shared with the new branch.
//   Pass: .len() on a %OoResS emits @oo_chars_len.
//   Fail: any IR that drops `recv` or has wrong byval size.
//
// Acceptance:
//   1. Fixture: let r = "x".to_string(); let n = r.len();
//      Drive emit-llvm; grep output for "@oo_chars_len".
//   2. llc -filetype=null on the output, exit 0.
//   3. Existing `.len()` on String literal still emits @oo_chars_len.
//
// Rollback: git checkout HEAD -- ooda/oodac/llvm_emit_method.oo.

// BUG 3 — ret_arc UAF on `return out` of %OoSList (HIGH)
//
// ret_arc releases every ARC local, then rets the same register.
// load_expand does `return out` where out is %OoSList. After
// ret_arc the slot is freed; the returned register dangles.
// A dangling list can make load_source look empty, surfacing
// as `ERR\tcheck\tempty` (plan_llvm_mem.oot:76).
//
// Evidence:
//   openOODA/audit/plan_llvm_mem.oot:22-23 names the residual.
//   :67-68 confirms C does retain first; LLVM does not.
//   :83-85 names the path: `return out` of a %OoSList local is
//     HIGH; ret_arc releases `out` then rets it; load_expand does
//     that. :117-123 puts the fix in ret_arc / stmt.
//
// Fix:
//   File: ooda/oodac/llvm_emit_stmt.oo (owns ret_arc; if named
//   differently, locate `fn llvm_emit_ret_arc` or `pub fn ret_arc`).
//   Action: pass the returned value's slot name into ret_arc.
//   For each ARC slot, if slot_name == ret_name, emit
//   `oo_<ty>_retain`; else emit `oo_<ty>_release` as before.
//   Pass: emit-llvm of `let out = [1,2,3]; return out;` produces
//     a slist_retain immediately before the ret, and zero
//     slist_release for `out`.
//   Fail: any release for the returned value, or a missing retain.
//
// Acceptance:
//   1. emit-llvm on the fixture above.
//   2. grep output: `slist_retain` appears; `slist_release` for
//      `%out` does NOT appear.
//   3. llc -filetype=null, exit 0.
//   4. C product path still passes (C already retains first).
//
// Rollback: git checkout HEAD -- ooda/oodac/llvm_emit_stmt.oo.

// BUG 4 — wasm_fn_println_lit helper never added (HIGH)
//
// wasm_phalanx.oot §3 line 35 names
//   pub fn wasm_fn_println_lit(src, fname) -> String
// returning the literal inside a body that is only
// `println("...");`. The helper is never defined or imported.
// wasm_emit.oo's pick_print / pick_if fall back to dummy `end`
// when the body is not a one-liner fold.
//
// Evidence:
//   openOODA/audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:33-35 names helper + contract.
//   openOODA/audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:43-45 puts DE2 on
//     ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fn.oo and wasm_emit_stmt.oo.
//   ooda/oodac/wasm_emit.oo:14-18 imports only token_fmt, fold,
//     pick_print, pick_if. No wasm_emit_fn / wasm_emit_stmt.
//   ooda/oodac/wasm_emit.oo:56-62 tries pick_print then pick_if;
//     neither is the phalanx helper.
//
// Fix:
//   File 1: ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fn.oo (new helper body; sibling
//     of wasm_emit_fold.oo and wasm_emit_pick_print.oo). Add three
//     small token_fmt walkers (wasm_fn_body, wasm_body_is_only_
//     println, wasm_println_lit) and the public entry that returns
//     the inside of the first STRING if the body is only
//     `println("...");`, else "".
//   File 2: ooda/oodac/wasm_emit.oo
//     - after line 18, add: import "wasm_emit_fn.oo";
//     - after line 62 (pick_if tail), inside the while body, add:
//         let mut lit2 = wasm_fn_println_lit(src, name);
//         if chars_len(lit2) > 0 { oo_wasm_set_fn_print(lit2); }
//   Pass: emit-wasm of `pub fn foo() { println("hi"); }` produces
//     a WASI fd_write of "hi\n" for `foo`.
//   Fail: empty literal, or WAT text in the binary.
//
// Acceptance:
//   1. Create ooda/fixtures/wasm_print_hi_helper.oo:
//        pub fn main() { foo(); }
//        pub fn foo() { println("hi"); }
//   2. ./oodac/oodac emit-wasm ooda/fixtures/wasm_print_hi_helper.oo
//        > /tmp/hi.wasm
//   3. od -An -tx1 -N8 /tmp/hi.wasm | grep -q 0061736d01000000.
//   4. wasmtime /tmp/hi.wasm prints "hi".
//   5. ! grep -q '(module' /tmp/hi.wasm.
//
// Rollback: git checkout HEAD -- ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fn.oo
//                    ooda/oodac/wasm_emit.oo

// BUG 5 — open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo missing (module refusal (MED)
//
// open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo asserts magic + file(1) but never
// refuses WAT text. Every other wasm_*.oo smoke in the suite
// uses `! grep -q '(module' <wasm>`. wasm_harn.oot §3 line 42
// requires the binary contain no WAT text. The fix is unrecorded.
//
// Evidence:
//   ooda/scripts/open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo:46-53 has only od magic
//     + file WebAssembly. No `'(module'` grep.
//   ooda/scripts/wasm_wat_honest_smoke.oo:35 is the canonical
//     pattern: `! grep -q '(module' <wasm>`.
//   openOODA/audit/wasm_harn.oot:42-43 requires no WAT text.
//   openOODA/audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:63 names this fix as HARN.
//
// Fix:
//   File: ooda/scripts/open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo
//   Action: between line 49 and line 50, insert:
//     if expect_quiet(p, "! grep -q '(module' " + wasm).is_err() {
//         println("FAIL wat");
//         process_exit(1);
//     }
//   Update the Beats comment at lines 7-11 to add a beat
//   "(no WAT text)".
//   Pass: smoke still PASS on the empty module from chs_rt_wasm.c.
//   Fail: a WAT regression that emits `(module` is now caught.
//
// Acceptance:
//   1. ./oodac/oodac run scripts/open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo stdout
//      ends with "open_wasm_binary_smoke: PASSED".
//   2. Pipe "(module" into /tmp/x.wasm; run the smoke against it;
//      must exit non-zero with "FAIL wat" on stdout.
//
// Rollback: git checkout HEAD -- ooda/scripts/open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo.

